# Maven build output. The shipped artifact is V71/script/sos-extended-boostables.jar
# (the deploy target the game loads from), which stays tracked on purpose.
#
# Tracking target/ was actively harmful: restoring its .class files with `git checkout`
# gives them mtimes newer than the sources, so maven-compiler-plugin skips recompiling
# and `install` silently re-jars stale bytecode. Never `mvn clean` here (the clean plugin
# is pointed at the project root) — delete target/classes by hand if a rebuild is needed.
target/

# Per-user IDE state. The rest of .idea/ (compiler.xml, misc.xml, vcs.xml,
# Changelog.txt, SteamDesc.bbcode, ...) is shared project config and stays tracked.
.idea/workspace.xml

# --- Per-developer build config (feature/stealth-alertness-boostables, 2026-09-13) ---
#
# pom.xml carries MACHINE-SPECIFIC absolute paths in its <windows>/<linux> profiles:
# game.install.directory, game.workshop.directory and game.mod.uploader.directory.
# game.install.directory is read by the install-game-jar / install-game-sources-jar
# executions in the *validate* phase, so a pom pointing at another developer's Steam
# install fails the build before it compiles anything. That is exactly what landed on
# this branch (D:/Games/... vs C:/Gaming/...), so the pom is ignored here to stop those
# paths round-tripping between machines.
#
# NOTE: pom.xml is still TRACKED — .gitignore does not untrack an existing file. To make
# this take effect run, once, and then commit:
#     git rm --cached pom.xml
# That removes the pom from the branch, so every developer must keep a local copy. If you
# would rather keep the pom shared, revert this entry and move the three paths into
# ~/.m2/settings.xml properties (or a -D override) instead.
pom.xml

# Eclipse project metadata. This project builds with Maven and is worked on in IntelliJ;
# these were added on this branch by an Eclipse user and are per-developer state.
# Also still tracked - untrack with:
#     git rm --cached .classpath .project -r .settings
.classpath
.project
.settings/
